UID:10000135-1797584400-1797589800@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Trail Talks with TLC: Brumley South
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC Executive Director\, Sandy Sweitzer\, for a walk at her favorite part of Brumley Nature Preserve.\nIf you are a hiker or birder who has avoided Brumley South because of the mountain bikers\, join us! You’ll discover dedicated walking trails with cool rock formations\, beautiful hardwood forests\, and just enough hills to make it fun – all without worrying about a biker whizzing past. Sandy will share the history of the preserve\, this expansion\, and plans for possible future expansions. She’ll also share some highlights of the grand opening almost 10 years ago and how it has transformed TLC’s work. This event is free\, but preregistration is required.\n\n \n\n\n\nQuick Details:\n\n 	Hike Leader: Sandy Sweitzer\, TLC Executive Director\n 	Preserve Name & Planned Trails: Brumley Nature Preserve\, University Station Road entrance\n 	Distance & Speed: 90 minutes\, slow to moderate\n 	Age Group: 12 and older\n 	Dogs: Narrow trails may not be best for furry friends\n\n\n\n\n\nIf registration is full\, please fill out the waitlist form here by December 16th at noon.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-brumley-south
LOCATION:Brumley South- University Station Entrance\, 3501 University Station Rd\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
