UID:10000136-1797865200-1797872400@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Winter Solstice Bird Walk
DESCRIPTION:Welcome the winter season with the birds of Brumley North!\nCross the bridge into winter as evening birding peaks at Brumley North at the exact moment the winter solstice occurs! Back by popular demand\, the winter solstice bird walk led by TLC Trail Guide\, Patrick D\, will unite patrons of the Tri-County Conservationists chapter of the North Carolina Wildlife Federation with TLC supporters in its second year in a row!\n\nWhite-throated sparrows\, eastern bluebirds\, Carolina wrens\, and more avian residents of the preserve will sound off the transition from autumn to winter as the shortest day of the year comes to a close and the longest night of the year begins. Hikers will be invited to ground themselves at TLC's Healing Labyrinth and admire its American Beautyberries\, known to attract hermit thrushes and other birds. You will then be led through the pines of Cemetery Connector Trail out to the bridge to complete Dairy Farm Trail\, then return back the way we came. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required.\n\n\n\nQuick Details:\n\n 	Hike Leader: Patrick D.\, TLC Trail Guide\n 	Preserve Name & Planned Trails: Brumley North Nature Preserve; Cemetery Connector\, Dairy Farm Trail\n 	Distance & Speed: 1.3 miles\, slow pace\n 	Age Group: 12 and older\n 	Extras: Bring binoculars\, comfortable warm clothes\, and flashlights\, as our hike will conclude in the dusk!\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \nIf registration is full\, please fill out the waitlist form here by December 17th at noon.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/winter-solstice-bird-walk-2
LOCATION:Brumley North Nature Preserve\, 3620 Old State Highway 10\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Birding,Hike
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
